From: ButterflyOS developers
Subject: [PATCH] usb: release autopm reference only after successful acquisition

usb_autopm_get_interface() uses pm_runtime_resume_and_get(), which rolls back
its increment on failure. The driver nevertheless set autopm_cnt to one,
then put that nonexistent reference at disconnect. This produces a Runtime
PM usage count underflow when the Flip radio is removed for deep suspend.

Record ownership only on success. Preserve the existing probe failure policy,
legacy-kernel branches and radio suspend/resume sequencing.

--- a/os_dep/linux/usb_intf.c
+++ b/os_dep/linux/usb_intf.c
@@ -1279,11 +1279,23 @@
 #endif
 	/* 2012-07-11 Move here to prevent the 8723AS-VAU BT auto suspend influence */
 #if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(2, 6, 33))
-	if (usb_autopm_get_interface(pusb_intf) < 0)
+#ifdef CONFIG_BT_COEXIST
+	/* A failed get rolls back its usage count in the USB core. Only a
+	 * successful acquisition may be released during adapter teardown.
+	 */
+	dvobj_to_pwrctl(dvobj)->autopm_cnt = 0;
+#endif
+	if (usb_autopm_get_interface(pusb_intf) < 0) {
 		RTW_INFO("can't get autopm:\n");
-#endif
+	} else {
+#ifdef CONFIG_BT_COEXIST
+		dvobj_to_pwrctl(dvobj)->autopm_cnt = 1;
+#endif
+	}
+#else
 #ifdef CONFIG_BT_COEXIST
 	dvobj_to_pwrctl(dvobj)->autopm_cnt = 1;
+#endif
 #endif
 
 	/* set mac addr */
